      "content": "Yes — the hesitation reflects his reluctance to use their savings for the journey. You have moved beyond the words “I shall go” and considered what he is deciding.\n\n**Model Answer:** Stephen is unsure as he does not want to use their savings to go to Johannesburg.\n\n### 📖 Concept & Thought Process (How to Understand It):\n* **The Concept / Rule:** Tone is the attitude or feeling conveyed by the speaker’s words. A phrase such as “Let me see” can suggest hesitation or uncertainty, especially when the speaker is weighing a decision.\n* **The Thought Process (How to Unpack It):**\n  1. Read the whole line, not just “I shall go”.\n  2. Notice that “Let me see” sounds like he is considering his choice.\n  3. Connect that hesitation to the situation: he is reluctant to use their savings for the trip to Johannesburg.\n* **How DBE Markers Score It:** The memo awards credit for identifying that Stephen is unsure and linking his uncertainty to not wanting to use their savings to go to Johannesburg. Include both parts for a complete response.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Do not decide a speaker’s tone from one word alone. Read the full phrase and connect the tone to the situation in the text."
